<title>GERMANY: Germany sees 1997 total tax revenues down 10.3 bln.</title>
<headline>Germany sees 1997 total tax revenues down 10.3 bln.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German Finance Ministry gave the following data on expected tax revenues according to the latest half-year estimate by an official working group:</p>
<p>(In billions of marks</p>
<p>				  1996     1997</p>
<p> Public sector (1)	  805.0    822.2</p>
<p> Change from May est.     - 5.0    -10.3</p>
<p>Breakdown by authority:</p>
<p> Federal			340.6    344.9</p>
<p> Change from May	    - 3.0    - 5.0</p>
<p>NOTE - The ministry said that changes to federal tax laws brought in an additional 2.9 billion marks in revenues in 1996, and transfers from European Union taxes created additional revenue of 700 million marks for the federal government. The revenue from the EU was offset by an equal addition to transfers to the EU.  </p>
<p>				  1996     1997</p>
<p> States			 330.5    335.9</p>
<p> Change from May est.     - 1.1    - 3.9</p>
<p> Local govts		   94.0     98.9</p>
<p> Change from May est.     - 0.6    - 1.0</p>
<p> Transfers to EU	     39.9     42.5</p>
<p> Change from May est.	-0.3     -0.4</p>
<p>NOTE - (1) Federal, state and local government tax revenues plus transfers to the European Union.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
